NOVELTY
-------

VISION

1) The camera system works with any low-cost 2D camera, unlike standard setups that rely on high-end cameras and proprietary integration software.
2) The system provides a built-in workflow to connect and perform different tasks without requiring users to manually write code.
3) The camera system is easy to set up, with minimal effort. Calibration and object tracking are handled internally, making it user-friendly.


ARCHITECTURE

1) Existing systems such as MotoSim are proprietary and have a steep learning curve. Our system is simpler, easier to use, and can be extended or updated based on user needs.
2) The system is designed for users with little to no programming knowledge and features a simple control dashboard-like interface.


SOFTWARE

1) The software can be easily deployed on both Windows and Linux using containerization.
2) It provides a plug-and-play mechanism, reducing the complexity of integrating sensors with industrial robots.


ULTRASONIC

1) The system supports multiple emergency stops by processing data from multiple sensors and triggering a stop when required.
2) The distance between the user and the robot workspace can be manually set and dynamically adjusted for each sensor.


LAN

1) LAN allows high data transfer between the software and robot, enabling better control over the system.
2) The risk of electrical shock is much lower with LAN (~1–5V) compared to Digital I/O (~24V DC).
